# Gold spammers (AutonomousGoldSpammers), the way 2003 had them: a throwaway character with a gibberish name floods
# /faction with gold ads, the realm reacts, a GM bans it, and a new one turns up later with a new name. {site} is a fake
# website the server makes up ("g 0 l d g 0 b l i n . c 0 m"); every ad names it. {target} is the spammer's name in the
# realm's reactions; the tells call the player "friend". No real website, company or payment service is
# named, and no real price is compared. Real swear words are not in the corpus: the realm swears the way 2003 chat did.
# New writing.

